[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two findings from validating the harness itself:
[0m[49m[39m  39, 48[0m:[39m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;9m- 40    [0m:[38;5;9m[49m **Status: PARITY REACHED — 0 missing symbols.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. **`cargo test` does NOT rebuild a `crate-type = ["cdylib"]` artifact.** The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    test binaries never link it, so a plain `cargo test` silently validates a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    *stale* `.so`. An injected bug initially "passed" 35/35 for this reason.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    Fixed two ways: `verify.sh` always runs `cargo build` before `cargo test`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    and `tests/differential.rs::assert_so_fresh` refuses to run if `src/lib.rs`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    is newer than the `.so`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. **Mutation sweep** (`mutation_check.sh`): 17 plausible translation bugs
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    injected into `src/lib.rs`; **15 caught** (6–31 failing tests each). The 2
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    survivors — `b2 & 0xf → 0x1f` and `b3 & 0x3 → 0x7` — are *semantically
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    equivalent mutants*, not blind spots: Rust's `<<` on `u8` discards bits
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    shifted past bit 7 without any overflow check, so the extra mask bits land at
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    bit ≥ 8 and vanish. Confirmed equivalent under both `release` and `debug`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Width-safety proof (C `int` promotion vs Rust `u8` arithmetic)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The C computes the output bytes in promoted `int` and truncates on store to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `unsigned char *p`; the Rust computes them directly in `u8`. These agree for all
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inputs because `decode()` returns at most 63:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | expression | C max (int) | fits in `u8`? |
